The '''Central Thyo-Merinese languages''' are the a branch of the [[Thyo-Merinese languages]] historically spoken in the central reaches of the Auser River in [[Thyon]], now spread across much of [[Thyon]]. 

Central Thyo-Merinese languages include: 
* [[Thyonese language]] - one of the official languages of Thyon.
* [[Menese language]] - a nearly extinct language spoken in [[Melapo]].
* [[Lower Thyonese language]] - a regional language spoken in Southern Thyon.

